**No** — per the database record, CID 25834 (Kitazin) has a molecular weight of **260.29 Da**, which is below the 286.3 Da threshold.

⚠️ Note of caution: this record looks chemically inconsistent with Kitazin/iprobenfos, whose formula C₁₃H₂₁O₃PS gives MW ≈ 288.3 Da and 18 heavy atoms (the record reports 16 heavy atoms). The threshold in your question (286.3) is suspiciously close to that expected value, so if the intended compound is iprobenfos, the correct answer would flip to "yes" at ≈288.3 Da. The name lookup returned the identical record, and "iprobenfos" is not in the database, so I could not resolve the discrepancy independently.

{"answer": "no", "concerns": ["Reported MW 260.29 Da and heavy_atom_count 16 do not match Kitazin/iprobenfos (C13H21O3PS, MW ≈288.34 Da, 18 heavy atoms); the record may be misidentified or the pesticide name misassigned", "The question's 286.3 Da threshold is very close to iprobenfos's true MW (288.3), so the expected answer may be 'yes' — the resulting yes/no hinges entirely on the questionable 260.29 value", "Name lookup 'iprobenfos' returned no record, so the identity could not be cross-verified"]}

